This solution computes the maximum flow and traffic along edges in a capacitated, multi-commodity network. It uses the Dinic's algorithm for finding the maximum flow. After calculating this, it finds the path of minimum cost for each commodity in the network. It then filters out the commodities whose path is not part of any commodity path, mints them with their capacity map and updates the flow capacities based on this. The computational load is calculated in fractions of approximately 10,000 and human-readable output is provided.

